; AUG 02
; Additional code to look for in-built extensions. These are signalled
; by the 6-bytes marker ((TZ>>. We search in the area between the vector table
; and the names.
;
; The form of extensions is:
;
; long wd wd    wd  . . . long wd wd    wd
; ____________________________________________________________
; | ((TZ>> |   ptr0  | a0 | b0 |< file >|  ptr1  | a1 | b1 | ...
;
; ptri is a relative long word pointer to the next file. The ai, bi are
; the relative addresses to the initialisation code and definitions
; respectively.
;
; The end is marked by a word -1.
;
; If extensions are found they will be initialised if needed.
;
; From version 5.35 extensions can contain a call to insert an _INS file.
; This is signalled by a0 = 1. Such an "extension" must be ignored.
