;
; The additional instructions allow returned int and fp parameters
; by setting the address of the actual variables instead of the adddress of
; a copied value. The marker for this is stored in bit 3 of the type code
; which has to be cleared in the "name table" after being used as a marker.
;
; The additional instructions also allow for array parameters.
; The possible values of the 1st byte of "type" are:
; 0 integer or fp variable (no value yet)
; 2 integer or fp variable
; 3 integer, fp or string array
;
; To mark "array" bit 2 of the type code is set.
;
