;
; Here we set a BASIC descriptor instead of a Turbo one.
;
; Turbo descriptor:
;
; Long word  Long word   Wd  Wd Wd       Wd
; ______________________________________________________________________________
; |  p  |  s    |   n-z  |  d(n)  | d(n-1) | . .  | d(0) |
;
; p      = pointer to values (absolute)
; s      = space needed for items
; n      = number of dimensions - 1
; z      = 1 for strings : 0 otherwise
; d(i)   = size of dimension i (eg DIM v%(3) would have d(0) = 4)
;
;
; BASIC descriptor - in terms of the Turbo items
;
; Long word     Wd    Wd   Wd  Wd Wd        Wd Wd
; _________________________________________________________________________________________
; |  p'        |   n' | d'(0)  |  m(0)  | d'(1)  | m(1)   | . .  |d'(n'-1)| m(n'-1)|
;
; p'     = p (pointer to values relative to BV_VVBAS)
; n'     = n+1
; d'(i)  = d(i)-1  [d'(n) = d(n)-2 for strings]
; m(i-1) = d(i)*m(i)
; m(n)   = 1
;
; We allow slicing by amending the BASIC descriptor.
; The information comes as follows. If there is an array there follows an array marker.
; The array marker is one word:
; Case A    0 means a bare array variable.
; Case B   +n means 2*n words follow indicating the slicing for each of the n arrays.
; Case C   -n means  n  words follow indicating one array item to be passed by reference.
;
; If the array is a string, and the last dimension is not accessed, this is signalled
; by -2 instead of the normal slice number.
;
; Where a slice ends with TO, the last item is sent by Parser_task as -1. This
; represents the maximum. Although the usual Turbo marker is 0, this has to be
; changed here to allow the slice 0,0 to be set.
;
; Action for each case is:
; Case A
; Set the appropriate BASIC descriptor for the variable and set its address in the Name Table.
; Case B
; Set the appropriate BASIC descriptor for the slice and set its address in the Name Table.
; If the descriptor collapses to a single value, the case is treated as for C.
; Case C
; Set the address of the item in the array in the Name Table so that it appears as a reference parameter.
;
m_p_d3:
